---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Copywriting Frameworks"
  description="Master the proven copywriting frameworks used by the world's best copywriters. AIDA, PAS, PASTOR, Hook-Story-Offer, and more—with guides on when and how to use each."
>
  <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
    Copywriting frameworks are the structures that make persuasion repeatable. Learn them, and you'll never stare at a blank page again.
  </p>

  <h2>The Essential Frameworks</h2>
  
  <p>
    These are the foundational frameworks every copywriter should know. Each serves different purposes and audiences.
  </p>

  <h3>AIDA (Attention → Interest → Desire → Action)</h3>
  <p>
    The grandfather of all copywriting frameworks. Captures attention, builds interest, creates desire, and prompts action. Works for almost any format.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/aida-framework-blog-content">AIDA Framework for Blog Content</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/aida-framework-for-saas">AIDA Framework for SaaS</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/aida-framework-for-financial-advisors">AIDA Framework for Financial Advisors</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>PAS (Problem → Agitation → Solution)</h3>
  <p>
    Start with the problem, twist the knife to make it urgent, then present your solution. Incredibly effective for pain-point marketing.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/problem-agitate-solution-blog-posts">PAS Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/pas-framework-for-coaches">PAS Framework for Coaches</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/pas-framework-for-lawyers">PAS Framework for Lawyers</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>PASTOR (Problem → Amplify → Story → Transformation → Offer → Response)</h3>
  <p>
    An expanded framework perfect for longer content. Adds storytelling and transformation to the classic problem-solution structure.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/pastor-framework-blog-posts">PASTOR Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Hook-Story-Offer (Russell Brunson)</h3>
  <p>
    The modern funnel framework. Hook their attention, tell a story that builds connection, then make an offer. Popularized by ClickFunnels.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/hook-story-offer-blog-posts">Hook-Story-Offer for Blog Posts</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/hook-story-offer-for-course-creators">Hook-Story-Offer for Course Creators</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/hook-story-offer-when-it-works">When Hook-Story-Offer Works (and When It Doesn't)</a></li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-12" />

  <h2>Additional Frameworks</h2>
  
  <p>
    Beyond the essentials, these frameworks offer specialized approaches for specific situations.
  </p>

  <h3>Before-After-Bridge (BAB)</h3>
  <p>
    Paint the current state, show the desired future state, then bridge the gap with your solution. Simple and visual.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/before-after-bridge-blog-posts">Before-After-Bridge for Blog Posts</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/before-after-bridge-for-real-estate">Before-After-Bridge for Real Estate</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>FAB (Features → Advantages → Benefits)</h3>
  <p>
    Translate product features into advantages, then into reader benefits. Essential for product-focused copy.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/fab-framework-blog-posts">FAB Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4 Ps (Promise → Picture → Proof → Push)</h3>
  <p>
    Make a promise, paint a picture of the outcome, prove it works, then push for action.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/4ps-framework-blog-posts">4 Ps Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>PPPP (Picture → Promise → Prove → Push)</h3>
  <p>
    A variation that leads with the picture before the promise. Good for visual storytelling.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/pppp-framework-blog-posts">PPPP Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>ACCA (Awareness → Comprehension → Conviction → Action)</h3>
  <p>
    Focuses on the cognitive journey from awareness to action. Good for educational content.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/acca-framework-blog-posts">ACCA Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>QUEST (Qualify → Understand → Educate → Stimulate → Transition)</h3>
  <p>
    Qualifies the reader first, then takes them on a journey. Great for targeted, high-intent content.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/quest-formula-blog-posts">QUEST Formula for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Star-Chain-Hook</h3>
  <p>
    Star (attention-grabbing opening) → Chain (logical sequence of facts/benefits) → Hook (call to action).
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/star-chain-hook-framework">Star-Chain-Hook Framework</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>StoryBrand (Donald Miller)</h3>
  <p>
    Position your customer as the hero and your brand as the guide. Story structure for marketing.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/storybrand-framework-blog-posts">StoryBrand Framework for Blog Posts</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>SLAP (Stop → Look → Act → Purchase)</h3>
  <p>
    Designed for short-form copy—ads, social posts, quick-hit content.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/slap-framework-short-copy">SLAP Framework for Short Copy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Soap Opera Sequence</h3>
  <p>
    Multi-email storytelling framework that builds suspense and connection over time.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/soap-opera-sequence-emails">Soap Opera Sequence for Emails</a></li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-12" />

  <h2>Headline Frameworks</h2>
  
  <p>
    Frameworks specifically for crafting headlines that stop readers.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/headline-formulas-blog-posts">Headline Formulas for Blog Posts</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/how-to-write-headlines">How to Write Headlines That Convert</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/direct-response-headlines">Direct Response Headlines</a></li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-12" />

  <h2>Choosing the Right Framework</h2>
  
  <p>
    Not sure which framework to use? Here's a quick guide:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Blog posts:</strong> AIDA, PAS, or PASTOR</li>
    <li><strong>Sales pages:</strong> PASTOR, Hook-Story-Offer</li>
    <li><strong>Email sequences:</strong> Soap Opera, PAS</li>
    <li><strong>Social media:</strong> SLAP, BAB</li>
    <li><strong>Landing pages:</strong> AIDA, 4 Ps</li>
    <li><strong>Product descriptions:</strong> FAB, BAB</li>
    <li><strong>About pages:</strong> StoryBrand, Hook-Story-Offer</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="mt-8">
    <a href="/copywriting-legends" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 font-medium">
      → Learn from the Copywriting Legends
    </a>
  </p>
  
  <p class="mt-4">
    <a href="/blog" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 font-medium">
      ← Browse all blog posts
    </a>
  </p>

  <CTASection />
</PageLayout>
